hypotheticals.analysis:
Step 1 — Identify the provision. The correct current-law cite is BNS s. 4 (Punishments), Chapter II — Of Punishments.
Step 2 — State the legal test in your own words, then list the ingredients:
   (1) The punishments to which offenders are liable under the provisions of this Sanhita are
   (2) (b) Imprisonment for life;
   (3) (c) Imprisonment, which is of two descriptions, namely:—
   (4) (1) Rigorous, that is, with hard labour;
   (5) (d) Forfeiture of property;
Step 3 — Check limitations, provisos and the rest of the Chapter so you do not apply s. 4 in a vacuum.
Step 4 — Map each fact to an ingredient. Write “this fact proves ingredient (a)” or “this fact is missing, so the section is not made out”.
Step 5 — Conclude. If every essential ingredient is proved and no exception covers the case, BNS s. 4 applies. If any essential ingredient fails, say so and stop. Do not invent a different section to save the answer.
